  "rationale": "structural: The structural obligations in `requirements.sdk.outlines.Outline` are: the `#[non_exhaustive]` struct `Outline` with public fields `items: Vec<OutlineItem>` and `diagnostic: Option<OutlineError>`; the `Outline::new(items: Vec<OutlineItem>) -> Self` signature; and the `Clone` and `Debug` trait implementations. Each has a concrete root.\n\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/contents.rs#struct[Outline]` has `#[derive(Clone, Debug)]` and `#[non_exhaustive]`. It declares `pub items: Vec<OutlineItem>` and `pub diagnostic: Option<OutlineError>`. A different field type, a missing attribute, or a missing derive would break the stated declaration even if runtime results were the same. This covers the type, fields, attribute and trait implementations.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/contents.rs#impl[Outline]#1/fn[new]` has the prescribed signature and sets `diagnostic: None`, as the text says `Outline::new` initializes it.\n\nThe remaining clauses describe behavior or meaning: the items come from a single parse, include the root, and `diagnostic` holds the first syntax error. These are not structural obligations on these roots. Both roots are marked `{impl}` for the requirement, and I found no uncovered root that needs a reference.\n\nbehavioral: The reviewed tests cover each behavioral obligation of `requirements.sdk.outlines.Outline`.\n\n- **Selectable items, including the whole-file root.**\n  - `tests/outline_content.rs#fn[rust_items_attach_documentation_and_preserve_structural_hashes]` asserts the exact selector list (root first), the kinds, and that the root span covers the whole source.\n  - `fn[unknown_extensions_keep_nonblank_lines_and_content_selectors]` checks the root span and item count for plain text, including the empty file.\n  - `fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` runs a `check` helper over every bundled language. I did not read that helper, but the Rust and plain-text tests already cover the obligation.\n- **`diagnostic` holds the first syntax error during recovery.**\n  - `src/outline/tests.rs#fn[reports_recovered_syntax_errors_with_lines]` asserts the reported error position for Rust and asserts the Python diagnostic is `Some`. It uses a TOML source with two errors and asserts the earlier one is reported, so it checks \"first\".\n  - `fn[recovered_outlines_keep_the_diagnostic_and_intact_items]` asserts the position and message, that intact items remain, and that `languages::Rust.outline` returns the same diagnostic.\n- **`diagnostic` is `None` for a clean parse.** `fn[rust_items_attach_documentation_and_preserve_structural_hashes]` ends by asserting the outline's diagnostic is `None`.\n- **`Outline::new` initializes `diagnostic` to `None`.** `fn[outline_constructors_preserve_fields_and_replace_attachments]` asserts `Outline::new(...).diagnostic.is_none()` and that the `items` field is preserved.\n- **`Clone` and `Debug`.** The same constructor test formats the outline with `Debug` and clones it, then asserts the cloned items' fields.\n- **Struct shape.** `#[non_exhaustive]` and the public field declarations are structural. `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the public export inventory.\n\nI found no behavioral gap.",
